# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Never commit .env.local.

# --- Supabase ---
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL: your project URL, e.g. https://<ref>.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY: the anon / publishable key (sb_publishable_...).
# Both are public (they ship in the browser bundle); Row Level Security protects data.
# Without these the app runs as an anonymous prototype: sync says "on this device
# only" and /verify/<id> says verification is unavailable. Nothing is faked.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Server-only. Bypasses RLS, never expose to the browser (currently unused).
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Export assistant (/sell) ---
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY: server-only. The assistant runs claude-haiku-4-5 and is
# rate-limited per signed-in account (see lib/assistant/protocol.ts). Without it
# the panel says the assistant is not configured for this deployment and refuses
# to answer; it never falls back to canned advice.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- EUDR deforestation screening (/sell) ---
# GFW_API_KEY: server-only, free, and issued over three HTTP requests rather
# than from a button in the web UI. docs/GFW-API-KEY.md has the exact calls,
# checked against the live OpenAPI spec; the short version is sign-up -> token
# -> POST /auth/apikey with an EMPTY `domains` list, because this app calls the
# API from the server and a server request sends no Origin header for a domain
# allowlist to match. Keys expire after a year. Needed only for the per-plot
# zonal statistics — the map layers are keyless public tiles.
# Without it the panel says the check cannot run and assumes nothing about the
# plot; it never reports zeros as "no deforestation found".
GFW_API_KEY=

# --- That is the whole list. ---
# Everything else this file used to carry is gone with the feature that needed it:
#   ANALYSIS_SERVICE_URL   — the in-house satellite service was deleted (PARKED.md).
#   CRON_SECRET            — the monitoring sweep cron was deleted.
#   ALERT_WEBHOOK_SECRET   — standing monitoring was deleted.
#   ACOUSTIC_INGEST_TOKEN  — the acoustic ingest route was deleted.
#
# The GROW lane needs no keys at all: Open-Meteo requires none, and the tea
# classifier runs in the browser from a static file in public/models/.
